  "rare_class_conclusion": "Coffee (101) and cardamom (11) are NATURALLY rare at the source: only 330 coffee and 38 cardamom government survey records enter matching across the five Dakshina Kannada taluks. Their pipeline retention is HIGHER than coconut/pepper (~30.6% / ~28.9% vs ~4.5% / ~7.8%) because coconut/pepper suffer an enormous duplicate-filter drop. No matcher stage is the bottleneck for the rare classes; recovering additional rare-class observations requires additional genuine source records, NOT looser matching.",
  "limitations": "est_imagery_candidates_wd180 is raster-existence date arithmetic only; point coverage / patch extraction are not modelled. env fields come from provenance.json (record key match); the join rate per class is reported explicitly."
